"stem": "<p>The diagram shows the life cycle of animal P with information provided.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_ACSJ/q28_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>egg → larva → pupa → adult (4 stages). Information box: The adult does not feed on wood but the larva does. / The adult lays its eggs in the cracks of wood.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>(a) State a difference between the larva and the pupa. [1]</p>\n<p>(b) Based on the information, give a reason why the adult lays its eggs in the cracks of wood? [1]</p>\n<p>A group of scientists studied the effect of temperature on the life cycle of animal P.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_ACSJ/q28_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>20°C→130 days; 25°C→100 days; 30°C→90 days.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>(c) How does the increase in temperature affect the length of the life cycle of animal P? [1]</p>",
"options": [],
"myAnswer": "(a) The larva feeds (and moves actively) but the pupa does not feed.\n  (b) The larva feeds on wood; when the egg hatches into a larva, it can start feeding on the wood immediately.\n  (c) As the temperature increases, the length of the life cycle decreases.",
"answer": "(a) The larva of P feeds but the pupa of P does not feed.\n  (b) When the egg hatches, P will become a larva, and the larva of P feeds on wood, so when the egg hatches, the larva of P can start feeding immediately.\n  (c) When the temperature increases, the length of the life cycle of P decreases.",
"keypoints": "(a) Comparison point: the larva feeds\n(a) the pupa does not feed\n(b) Logic chain: the egg hatches into a larva\n(b) the larva feeds on wood\n(c) the life cycle becomes shorter (decreases)",
