"stem": "<p>The following pictures show the development in the life cycle of a plant.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_ACSJ/q29_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A: seedling (with leaves and roots); B: germinating seed (root growing); C: mature plant with flowers; D: seed.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>(a) Order the pictures to show the correct sequence of growth in the life cycle of the plant, starting with picture A. [1]<br>A → ____ → ____ → ____</p>\n<p>(b) At which picture(s), A, B, C or D, can the plant make its own food? [1]</p>\n<p>(c) Name the stage of the plant in picture C. Explain your answer. [1]</p>\n<p>(d) State the conditions needed for seeds to germinate. [1]</p>",
"options": [],
"myAnswer": "(a) A → C → D → B\n  (b) C\n  (c) Adult stage（成株）。因为 C 已长出完全伸展的叶和花（fully developed leaves and flowers）。\n  (d) Water, oxygen and warmth.",
"answer": "(a) A → C → D → B\n  (b) C\n  (c) Adult stage. The adult stage will have fully developed leaves and flowers. C has fully developed leaves and flowers.\n  (d) Water, oxygen and warmth.",
"keypoints": "(c) Answer: adult stage + reason: it has fully developed leaves and flowers\n(d) All three conditions must be written: water\n(d) oxygen（air\n(d) warmth",
