"stem": "<p>Peter placed two balls, W and X, made of different materials into a tank of water.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_ACSJ/q31_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Ball W floats on the water; ball X sinks to the bottom.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>(a) Which ball, W or X, sank in the water? [1]</p>\n<p>(b) Name the property of materials tested by Peter. [1]</p>\n<p>The diagram shows a girl with a swimming board.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_ACSJ/q31_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>girl with swimming board (the swimming board floats on the water).</figcaption></figure>\n<p>(c) Peter said that the swimming board is made of the same material as ball W. Do you agree? Explain your answer. [1]</p>",
"options": [],
"myAnswer": "(a) Ball X.\n  (b) Buoyancy（ability to float or sink in water，浮沉性）。\n  (c) No. 其他材料也能浮在水上，浮在水上不代表是同一种材料（不能仅凭\"会浮\"下结论）。",
"answer": "(a) X\n  (b) Buoyancy\n  (c) No. There are other materials that can float on water.",
