"stem": "<p>A button magnet is attached to Mark's toy car as shown. When he brought metal rod X close to the button magnet, the toy car moved forward.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_ACSJ/q32_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Metal rod X is on the left; a button magnet is fixed to the front of the toy car and the car moves to the right (direction moved by toy car).</figcaption></figure>\n<p>(a) Explain why the toy car moved forward when Mark brought metal rod X close to the button magnet attached to the car. [2]</p>\n<p>(b) The toy car did not move forward when Mark replaced metal rod X with object Y. Explain why. [1]</p>",
"options": [],
"myAnswer": "(a) X 是一块磁铁，且它的磁极与车上的按钮磁铁面向的一端是同极（like poles），同极相斥，排斥力把车推向前。\n  (b) Y 不是磁铁，对按钮磁铁没有排斥力，所以车不动。",
"answer": "(a) X is a magnet and the like poles of X and the (button) magnet is facing each other so they repelled.\n  (b) Y is not a magnet.",
"keypoints": "(a) Both scoring points are needed: (1) X is a magnet (is a magnet)\n(a) (2) like poles facing each other repel (like poles facing each other)\n(a) repel\n(b) Answer: Y is not a magnet",
