"kw": "",
"stem": "<p>Ravi wanted to find out how the number of strokes of a magnet on the nail affects its magnetic strength. He used the stroke method on four identical nails, A, B, C and D.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_ACSJ/q33_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Stroke the nail with the magnet in the same direction.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>He recorded the results in the table.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_ACSJ/q33_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A: 15 times→2 clips; B: 30 times→4 clips; C: 45 times→5 clips; D: 60 times→7 clips.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>(a) Name a material that the nails can be made of. [1]</p>\n<p>(b) Tick (✓) the variable(s) which must be kept the same for Ravi to carry out a fair test. [1]</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_ACSJ/q33_fig3.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Variables：Type of nail / Type of magnet / Number of strokes / Direction of strokes / Number of paper clips attracted。</figcaption></figure>\n<p>(c) Name another method that Ravi can use to make the iron nails into magnets. [1]</p>",
"figAnswer": {"fig": 2, "parts": {"b": "text"}, "boxes": []},
"options": [],
"myAnswer": "(a) Iron（铁；钢也可以）。\n  (b) 勾：Type of nail、Type of magnet、Direction of strokes。\n  (c) Electrical method（用电：把导线绕在钉上通电 / 用电磁铁方法）。",
"answer": "(a) Cobalt. (cobalt; magnetic materials such as iron/steel are also acceptable, official answer gives Cobalt)\n  (b) Type of nail / Type of magnet / Direction of strokes (tick all three).\n  (c) Electrical method.",
