"marks": 3.0,
"topicRaw": "Magnets",
"topic": "Interactions",
"subtopic": "Magnets",
"difficulty": 4,
"kw": "",
"stem": "<p>Rami placed two button magnets over a worksheet on the whiteboard as shown.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_ACSJ/q34_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Button magnets hold the worksheet on the whiteboard.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>When she brought the two button magnets close to each other, they moved away.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_ACSJ/q34_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>The left magnet is marked South (on the outer side) and its facing pole is pole X; the facing pole of the right magnet is pole Y; the two arrows show them moving apart (repelling).</figcaption></figure>\n<p>(a) Name poles X and Y. [1]<br>X: ______  Y: ______</p>\n<p>Rumi wanted to find out how the size of button magnets affects their magnetic strength. She conducted an investigation using three different-sized magnets, A, B and C as shown.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_ACSJ/q34_fig4.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A is the largest, B is medium, C is the smallest.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>She kept adding more worksheets until both the worksheets and magnets fell off the whiteboard. She recorded her results in the table as shown.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_ACSJ/q34_fig3.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Number of worksheets held before falling off：A：5；B：8；C：10。</figcaption></figure>\n<p>(b) Which magnet, A, B or C, is the strongest? Explain your answer based on the results. [1]</p>\n<p>(c) Rumi concluded that the size of a magnet does not affect its magnetic strength. Explain why she made this conclusion based on the results for magnet A. [1]</p>",
"options": [],
"myAnswer": "(a) X: North；Y: North（两磁铁相斥 → 相对的两极是同极；左磁铁外端为 South，故面向端 X 为 North，则 Y 也应为 North）。注：官方答案为 X: North, Y: South，与\"同极相斥\"的推理不一致，已照录官方。\n  (b) C。它掉落前夹住的工作纸最多（10 张），说明磁力最强。\n  (c) 虽然 A 最大，但它在掉落前夹住的工作纸最少（5 张，只有 C 的一半），说明大小最大磁力反而最弱，所以尺寸不影响磁力。",
"answer": "(a) X: North. Y: South.\n  (b) C. C held the most number of worksheets before falling off, therefore, C is the strongest.\n  (c) Although A is the biggest, it held the least number of worksheets before falling off. (handwritten addition: half the least number of worksheets before falling off)",
"keypoints": "(a) According to the official answer: X: North\n(a) Y: South\n(a) and state the reason as like poles repel\n(b) Answer: C + reason: held the most worksheets before falling off (= strongest magnetic force)\n(c) Key sentence: although A is the biggest, it held the least number of worksheets (least number of worksheets)",
