"stem": "<p>Study the diagrams below carefully.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_ACSP/q28_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Left: life cycle of a grasshopper (stage K is the nymph); right: life cycle of a mosquito (stage L is the larva in water).</figcaption></figure>\n<p>(a) Based on the diagrams, state two differences between stage K and stage L. [2]<br>(b) Suggest a way to reduce mosquito breeding at stage L and state how it works. [2]</p>",
"options": [],
"myAnswer": "(a) (1) Stage K (nymph of grasshopper) looks like its adult, while stage L (mosquito larva) does not look like its adult. (2) Stage K lives on land while stage L lives in the water.\n  (b) Spray/pour a layer of oil on the stagnant water. This stops/blocks the breathing tube of stage L (the larva) so it cannot breathe and dies.",
"answer": "(a) Stage K of grasshopper looks like its adult while Stage L of mosquito does not look like its adult. / Stage K of grasshopper lives on **land** while Stage L of mosquito lives in the **water**. (any two differences accepted)\n  (b) Spray a layer of oil on the water. This **stops** the breathing tube of stage L and it cannot breathe.",
"keypoints": "(a) 1 mark for each difference\n(b) (2) principle (oil blocks the breathing tube of the wrigglers (mosquito larvae) so they cannot breathe / clearing stagnant water so the larvae cannot survive)",
