"stem": "<p>Ralph made an electromagnet.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_ACSP/q30_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Electromagnet set-up: a battery is connected to a coil wound on an iron rod, and paper clips are attracted to both ends.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>He conducted the experiment and recorded the results in the table below.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_ACSP/q30_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Table: Set-up A: 8 turns, 6 clips; B: 16 turns, X clips; C: 24 turns, 10 clips.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>(a) What is the aim of the experiment? [1]<br>(b) Based on his results, what is the likely value of X? [1]<br>(c) State the relationship between the number of turns around the iron rod and the strength of the electromagnet. [1]<br>(d) Without changing the number of turns around the iron rod, suggest another way to increase the number of paper clips attracted by the electromagnet. [1]</p>",
