"stem": "<p>Chris hung two objects, X and Y, at equal distance away from a suspended bar magnet. The diagram below shows how object X and Y interacted with the bar magnet. One of the objects is an iron bar while the other is a magnet.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_HenryPark/q34_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Object X (left) slants away from the magnet; the bar magnet is labelled with N and S poles; object Y (right) slants towards the magnet.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>a)  Based on the information provided, identify X and Y.  [2]<br>(i)  Object X: ____________<br>(ii)  Object Y: ____________<br>b)  Explain why object X and the bar magnet moved away from each other.  [1]<br>c)  State what Chris would have observed if object X is made of wood.  [1]</p>",
"options": [],
"myAnswer": "a) (i) Object X is a magnet.（它被磁铁排斥）(ii) Object Y is an iron bar.（它被磁铁吸引）\n  b) The like (same) poles of object X and the bar magnet were facing each other, so they repelled.\n  c) Nothing would happen — the bar magnet would not attract or repel the wooden object X (wood is non-magnetic).",
"answer": "a) (i) Non-magnetic; (ii) Magnetic; b) North North (like poles facing each other); c) If X is wood then the bar magnet and Y will attract.",
