"kw": "",
"stem": "<p>Muthu placed Bar magnet X in a tray of paper clips. The bar magnet has three parts, A, B and C. The diagram below shows what happened when he lifted the magnet up.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_HenryPark/q35_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>The two ends A and C of bar magnet X attract more paper clips, while the middle B has hardly any paper clips.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>a)  Based on the diagram above, describe what he observed when the bar magnet was lifted. Explain your answer.  [2]</p>\n<p>Muthu then placed Bar magnet X near Object Y. He observed that Object Y was attracted to Bar magnet X as shown below.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_HenryPark/q35_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>The S-pole end of bar magnet X is placed near end E of object Y, and Y is attracted towards X.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Muthu's sister told him that Object Y is a magnet.<br>b)  What should he do to find out if his sister is correct?  [2]</p>",
"options": [],
"myAnswer": "a) He observed that parts A and C (the two ends) attracted the most paper clips while part B (the middle) attracted the fewest/none. The magnetic force of a magnet is strongest at its two poles (ends).\n  b) Use Object Y to try to repel (not attract) another magnet — e.g. bring the ends of Object Y near a known magnet; if it can repel the magnet, Y is a magnet.（或：把 Object Y 用线悬挂起来，看它静止时是否指向南北方向。）",
"answer": "a) He observed that both sides have the same number of paper clips. Because A and C are magnetic. (i.e. more paper clips are attracted at the two ends and fewer in the middle, as the magnetism is strongest at the poles); b) Test by putting some paperclips near it and see if any is attracted to it.",
"keypoints": "The middle (B) has the least [1 mark]\nExplanation: the two ends (poles) of a magnet are the strongest [1 mark]\nb) Official answer: bring a paper clip near Object Y\nsee if it is attracted [2 marks]",
