"stem": "<p>Winnie wants to have a fish tank as shown below.<br>Winnie conducted an experiment shown below to find the best material to use to make part W for her to display her fishes for all to observe.<br>She used a torchlight and shone a light through three materials, P, Q and R as shown below.<br>She then recorded the amount of light that passed through the material in the bar graph shown below.<br>(a) Which material P, Q or R, is the most suitable to make Part W? [1]<br>(b) Give a reason for your answer in (a). [1]</p>\n<figure>- Diagram:<img src=\"images/EOY_MahaBodhi/q30_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A fish tank, with part W labelled (the viewing side/tank wall).</figcaption></figure>\n<figure>- Diagram:<img src=\"images/EOY_MahaBodhi/q30_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Experimental setup — a torch shines at a material (sheet).</figcaption></figure>\n<figure>- Diagram:<img src=\"images/EOY_MahaBodhi/q30_fig3.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Bar chart — amount of light passed through (units): P the highest, R next, Q the lowest.</figcaption></figure>",
"options": [],
