"subtopic": "Materials",
"difficulty": 2,
"kw": "",
"stem": "<p>Lily hung three strips of materials, X, Y and Z, on a string and placed one end of the strips in a basin of coloured water as shown below.<br>After some time, she took out the strips and measured the length of the strip that was stained in coloured water. The results were recorded in the table below.<br>(a) State the property of material that is tested in this experiment. [1]<br>(b) Based on the results, which material X, Y or Z, is most suitable to be used to make a raincoat? Explain your answer. [2]</p>\n<figure>- Diagram:<img src=\"images/EOY_MahaBodhi/q31_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Experimental setup — a retort stand holds a string, with the lower ends of material strips X, Y and Z dipped into coloured water in a basin.</figcaption></figure>\n<figure>- Diagram:<img src=\"images/EOY_MahaBodhi/q31_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Results table — Length of strip stained (cm): X=2, Y=5, Z=0.</figcaption></figure>",
"options": [],
