"answer": "(a) 3; (b) Both have 3 stages in its life cycle; (c) P – the frog have 3 stages in its life cycle (official answer).\n  - **Note/doubt**: The official answer gives P, but according to the table P's \"young resembles adult\" is ✓, while a frog's young (tadpole) clearly does not resemble its adult (the ✓ should be in R's row: young does not resemble adult ×, has three stages ✓). Scientifically R is more correct; when memorising from this question bank, score with the official answer P, but when explaining, it is advisable to point out this contradiction; the reason \"has 3 stages\" can earn partial credit.",
"keypoints": "(a) \"3 / three stages\"\n(a) b) Keyword \"both have 3 stages\"\n(a) c) Letter of the animal + reason \"has three stages in its life cycle\"\n(a) Must add \"young does not resemble the adult\" (more scientifically accurate",
