"stem": "<p>Jeslyn played with the toy shown below. (Part K floats above Part L)<br>She observed that part K is 'floating' above part L.<br>(a) Identify the objects that parts K and L are made of. [1]<br>Jeslyn attached bar magnet M to the top of a toy car using some tape and rolled the toy car towards another magnet, P, that was glued onto the wall. Before the front of the toy car reached the magnet P, Jeslyn observed that it started to move backwards.<br>(b) Explain why the toy car moved backwards. [2]</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_Nanyang/q31_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A toy with Part K floating above Part L.</figcaption></figure>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_Nanyang/q31_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Magnet M taped on top of a toy car; the car rolls towards magnet P stuck on the wall, with an arrow showing \"Toy car moved backwards\".</figcaption></figure>",
"options": [],
"myAnswer": "(a) Both parts K and L are magnets.（K 和 L 都是磁铁）\n  (b) The like poles of magnets M and P were facing each other, so they repelled. The repulsive force pushed the toy car backwards.（M 和 P 相对的是同名磁极，相互排斥，排斥力把车推后退。）",
"answer": "(a) Magnets\n  (b) The like poles of Magnets P and M are facing each other so they repelled.",
"keypoints": "(a) must write \"magnets\" (magnets\n(b) both points needed: ① \"like poles / like poles facing each other\" (like poles facing each other\n(b) ② \"repel / repulsion pushes the car backwards\" (they repel each other",
