"stem": "<p>Sally conducted an experiment to find out how well each material, P, Q, R and S, can absorb water.</p>\n<p>Each material was identical in size, length and thickness. She dipped one end of each material into a container of coloured water.</p>\n<p>At the end of the experiment, the height of the water level on each material was observed as shown below.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_Raffles/q35_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>\n<p>(a) Arrange and write down the materials, P, Q, R or S, in the box, starting from the non-absorbent to the most absorbent material. [1]</p>\n<p>Non-absorbent ______ → ______ → ______ → ______ Most absorbent</p>\n<p>The diagram below shows a mop.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_Raffles/q35_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>\n<p>(b) Using the information from your answer in part (a), which material, P, Q, R or S, is most suitable to make part A of a mop? Give a reason for your answer. [2]</p>",
