"stem": "<p>Devi wanted to find out if the number of turns of wire around a nail would affect the magnetic strength of an electromagnet. She prepared four set-ups, A, B, C and D, using similar wires, nails and batteries. [Figure: four electromagnet set-ups — A one battery with many turns of wire, B one battery with many turns of wire, C two batteries with many turns of wire, D two batteries with few turns of wire (see figure)] Which two set-ups should she use to ensure that a fair test was conducted?</p>\n<figure>- <img src=\"images/EOY_Rosyth/q24_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A and B use one battery; C and D use two batteries; the number of coils of wire differs for each</figcaption></figure>",
