"subtopic": "Fungi & Bacteria",
"difficulty": 3,
"kw": "",
"stem": "<p>Leon conducted an experiment with two similar apples, P and Q. He placed P in the refrigerator and Q on the table. After some days, he observed a few dark patches of X growing on Q as shown in the diagram below. His mother told him that the dark patches were living things. [Figure: apple P in the refrigerator is unchanged; apple Q on the table has dark patches X growing on it] (a) Which group of living things does X belong to? [1] (b) Based on his experiment, what can Leon conclude about the condition that X needs in order to grow? [1] Leon spotted living thing Y growing in his garden. Both X and Y reproduce in a similar way. [Figure: living thing Y (a fern-like plant)] (c) Leon claims that X and Y belong to the same group of living things. Based on the difference in how X and Y obtain their food, explain why he is wrong. [1]</p>\n<figure>- <img src=\"images/EOY_Rosyth/q27_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Apple P in the refrigerator has no dark patches; apple Q at room temperature has developed dark patch X</figcaption></figure>\n<figure>- <img src=\"images/EOY_Rosyth/q27_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Y is a green plant growing in the garden</figcaption></figure>",
"options": [],
"myAnswer": "(a) Fungi. (b) X needs warmth to grow. (c) Y (a plant) makes its own food, but X (a fungus) cannot make its own food; it feeds on other living things, so they are not in the same group.",
