"stem": "<p>The life cycles of animals A and B are shown below. [Figure: animal A is a grasshopper (3 stages: egg → nymph → adult); animal B is a beetle (4 stages: egg → larva → pupa → adult)] (a) State a difference between both life cycles. [1] (b) State a similarity between both life cycles. [1] (c) Both animals reproduce by laying many eggs. How does laying many eggs ensure the survival of their own kind? [1] (d) The table below compares the life cycles of animals A and C. [Table: Does it have a 3-stage life cycle? A: Yes, C: Yes; Does the life cycle take place on land only? A: Yes, C: No] Based on the table above, suggest what animal C is likely to be. [1]</p>\n<figure>- <img src=\"images/EOY_Rosyth/q29_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A is the 3-stage life cycle of a grasshopper; B is the 4-stage life cycle of a beetle</figcaption></figure>",
"options": [],
