"stem": "<p>Sunil wanted to carry out an experiment using the given apparatus to find out if materials, X and Y, float on water. [Figure: basin of water, materials X and Y] (a) Complete the table to show how Sunil should carry out his experiment. Write the steps 1, 2 or 3, in the boxes provided in the table. The last step has been done for you. [1] [Table: Step 4 is given: Repeat steps 2 and 3 with material Y. Steps to be ordered: Observe the position of the material in the basin of water. / Push material X to the bottom of the basin of water. / Fill the basin with water.] Sunil carried out the experiment and his results are as shown below. [Figure: both X and Y float on the water] He then placed identical weights on each material and observed the results as shown below. [Figure: X still floats, while Y and the weights on it sink in the water] (b) Based Sunil's results above, which object, X or Y, is more suitable for making the float? Explain your answer. [2]</p>\n<figure>- <img src=\"images/EOY_Rosyth/q31_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A basin of water and two materials, X and Y</figcaption></figure>\n<figure>- <img src=\"images/EOY_Rosyth/q31_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Both X and Y float on the water</figcaption></figure>\n<figure>- <img src=\"images/EOY_Rosyth/q31_fig3.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>After the same weight is placed on each, X still floats on the water while Y sinks</figcaption></figure>",
"options": [],
"myAnswer": "(a) 依次为 3、2、1（Observe=3；Push X=2；Fill the basin with water=1）。(b) X。X 即使加上重量仍能浮在水面，而浮具需要承受人的重量并保持漂浮。",
"answer": "(a) Observe＝**3**；Push material X＝**2**；Fill the basin with water＝**1**. (b) C: Material **X**. E: Material X floats even **when a weight is added**. R: A float needs to **support the weight of a person** and still float in water.",
