"stem": "<p>Bobby bought two fish J and K. He kept fish J in the kitchen and fish K in the freezer. He observed the amount of bacteria on both fish at the start and end of the experiment. He recorded the results of his experiment in the table below.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_StNicholas/q29_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>\n<p>(a) Based on his results, is the kitchen or the freezer a more suitable place to keep the fish fresh for a longer time? Explain your answer. [1]<br>(b) Name the instrument that Bobby used to observe the bacteria on the fish. [1]<br>(c) For his experiment to be fair, tick (✓) the variables that he should keep the same. [2]</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_StNicholas/q29_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>",
"options": [],
"myAnswer": "(a) The freezer. Fish K in the freezer had only 15 units of bacteria at the end, much fewer than Fish J in the kitchen (290 units), so bacteria grow more slowly at low temperature and the fish stays fresh longer.\n  (b) Microscope.\n  (c) Tick \"Type of fish used\" and \"Size of fish J and K\".",
"answer": "(a) The freezer. The amount of bacteria is less on Fish K at the end of the experiment.\n  (b) Microscope.\n  (c) Type of fish used and Size of fish J and K.",
"keypoints": "(a) freezer\n(a) fewer bacteria（15 vs 290）\n(a) bacteria grow slower at lower temperature / cold slows growth\n(b) microscope\n(c) Type of fish used\n(c) Size of fish J and K",
