"stem": "<p>The diagram below shows two stages in the life cycle of a mosquito. (Stages G and H are shown as adult mosquitoes)<br>- (a) Fill in the stages 'G' and 'H' correctly in the empty boxes below. [1]<br>- (b) Dengue fever is spread by adult female mosquitoes. To reduce dengue fever, special male mosquitoes were released to breed with female mosquitoes. Their eggs do not hatch. The diagram below shows what happened. Suggest how the release of the special male mosquitoes affect the life cycle of the mosquitoes. [1]<br>- (c) State another way to prevent mosquito breeding at home. [1]</p>\n<p>![Figure: adult mosquitoes (Stage G, Stage H) and the life cycle diagram (larva → pupa → [blank] → [blank] → larva)](images/EOY_TaoNan/q22_fig1.png)<br>Caption: in the life cycle diagram, the blank after pupa is G (adult) and the blank before larva is H (egg).</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_TaoNan/q22_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>After mating with the female mosquito, the special male mosquito produces eggs that do not hatch.</figcaption></figure>",
