"stem": "<p>The diagram below shows the human circulatory system.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_MGS/q27_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A diagram of the human circulatory system: Part W points to the heart and Part X points to a blood vessel in the leg.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>(a) Name Parts W and X of the human circulatory system. [1]<br>(b) Blood found in the human system above carries substances around the body. Name all the substances that are carried by the blood to all parts of the body. [1]<br>Study the car frame as shown in the diagram below.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_MGS/q27_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A car (car frame).</figcaption></figure>\n<p>(c) Name the human body system that serves the same function as the car frame. [1]<br>(d) How is the function of the car frame similar to the human body system you have identified in (c)? [1]<br>(e) What does the system identified in (c), together with the muscular system enable us to do? [1]</p>",
