"subtopic": "Materials",
"difficulty": 3,
"kw": "",
"stem": "<p>Lynn had three rulers made of different materials, X, Y and Z. She then measured the length each ruler could bend.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/EOY_MGS/q29_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Diagram of hands bending a ruler (length that the ruler bent); Table: Material X = 10 cm, Y = 1 cm, Z = 5 cm.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>She recorded the results as shown in the table below.<br>(a) Based on the results, which material X, Y or Z is the least flexible? Explain why. [1]<br>Lynn's brother wore a life vest during his canoeing practice.<br>(b) Based on the results, which material X, Y or Z is most suitable for a life vest? Explain why. [1]<br>(c) State a property of material that makes the canoe safe for its use. [1]</p>",
"options": [],
"myAnswer": "(a) Y. It bent the least (only 1 cm), so it is the least flexible.\n  (b) X. It is the most flexible (bent the most, 10 cm), so the life vest is the most comfortable to wear.\n  (c) It is able to float on water, so it will not sink.",
"answer": "(a) Y, because it bent the least out of the three materials, so it is the least flexible.\n  (b) X, as it is the most flexible as it bent 10 cm. Thus, it is the most comfortable for the user to wear the life vest.\n  (c) It is able to float on water, so it will not sink.",
"keypoints": "(a) Y\n(a) bent the least (bent only 1 cm) → least flexible\n(b) X\n(b) most flexible (bent 10 cm, bent the most) → most comfortable to wear\n(c) able to float on water / floats, so it will not sink",
