"kw": "",
"stem": "<p>Mary watered her plant every day and made sure that it had enough sunlight. She measured the height of her plant over four weeks.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA1_MahaBodhi/q9_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Measuring the height of plant of a potted plant.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>She recorded her findings in the graph below.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA1_MahaBodhi/q9_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>The bar chart shows the plant's height increasing week by week from Week 1 to Week 4.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>(a) (i) State the change in the height of the plant over the four weeks. [1]</p>\n<p>(ii) State the characteristics of living things shown by the plant based on her observation above. [1]</p>\n<p>(b) Mary was away on a holiday. After two weeks, she found that the plant has wilted as shown below.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA1_MahaBodhi/q9_fig3.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>After returning from a two-week holiday, the plant has wilted (wilted plant).</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Explain why the plant wilted after two weeks. [2]</p>",
