"stem": "<p>In an experiment, Sonya kept four identical slices of bread P, Q, R and S under different conditions as shown below.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA1_TaoNan/q9_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>The amount of water and temperature conditions for the four slices of bread</figcaption></figure>\n<p>After two weeks, Sonya counted the number of patches of mould on the four slices of bread. She recorded her observations in the table below.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA1_TaoNan/q9_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Bread S has the most mould patches (10 ml of water, 32 °C)</figcaption></figure>\n<p>(a) Based on the results, state the conditions for the most amount of mould to grow. [1]</p>\n<p>Conditions : ________ ml of water and ________ °C</p>\n<p>(b) Sonya then wanted to find out if the presence of light affects the growth of mould. She has 4 set-ups below each with bread of an identical size. Which 2 set-ups, A, B, C or D should she use so that she can conduct a fair test? [1]</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA1_TaoNan/q9_fig3.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A table comparing the conditions of the four set-ups</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Set-ups ________ and ________.</p>",
