"kw": "",
"stem": "<p>Jianfu set up the following experiment to find out which material allows the greatest number of books to be placed on it before it breaks.</p>\n<p>He used different materials, P, Q, R and S for the ramp and recorded the number of books placed on the material before it breaks in the table as shown.</p>\n<table><tbody><tr><td>Material</td><td>Number of books placed before it breaks</td></tr><tr><td>P</td><td>19</td></tr><tr><td>Q</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>R</td><td>15</td></tr><tr><td>S</td><td>8</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>(a) Name the property of materials that Jianfu is testing in his experiment. [1]</p>\n<p>(b) The picture shows a slide at an outdoor playground.<br>Which material, P, Q, R or S, is the most suitable to make part X of the slide? Explain your answer based on the results in the table. [1]</p>\n<p>(c) State one other property of the material used to make part X based on the use of the slide. [1]</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA2_ACSJ/q7_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Books placed on a ramp, with one end raised by a support</figcaption></figure>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA2_ACSJ/q7_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>An outdoor slide, with part X being the chute of the slide</figcaption></figure>",
"options": [],
"myAnswer": "(a) Strength（强度）.\n  (b) Material P. It can hold the most number of books (19) before it breaks, so it is the strongest. A slide must be as strong as possible so people can slide on it without breaking.\n  (c) Waterproof（滑梯在户外，需防水/防雨）.",
"answer": "(a) Strength.\n  (b) Material P. It can hold the most number of books before it broke. A slide must be as strong as possible in order for people to slide on it without breaking.\n  (c) Waterproof.",
"keypoints": "(a) Keyword \"strength\" (strength\n(b) Choose \"Material P\" + reason \"holds/breaks at the most number of books (19)\" (withstands the most books before breaking = strongest\n(c) Keyword \"waterproof\" (outdoor items need to be waterproof",
