"stem": "<p>Jamal conducted an experiment by placing a 1 kg weight on four strips made of different materials, J, K, L and M.</p>\n<p>He measured the distance bent by each material, d, and recorded his results in a graph as shown.</p>\n<p>(a) State the property of materials that is tested in this experiment. [1]</p>\n<p>(b) Jamal decided to use material K to make part Y of his belt.<br>(i) Give a reason why material K is the most suitable. [1]<br>(ii) State a property of the material used to make part Z based on the use of the belt. [1]</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA2_ACSJ/q8_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>The strip is clamped at both ends with a clamp, with a 1 kg weight hung in the middle; d is the distance bent</figcaption></figure>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA2_ACSJ/q8_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Bar chart of distance d (cm) for materials J, K, L and M; K has the largest distance bent, M the smallest</figcaption></figure>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA2_ACSJ/q8_fig3.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A belt, with part Y being the strap and part Z being the buckle part</figcaption></figure>",
"options": [],
"myAnswer": "(a) Flexibility（柔韧性）.\n  (b)(i) Material K bends the most (largest d), so it is the most flexible. A belt (part Y) must be flexible to wrap around a person's waist.\n  (b)(ii) Strength（扣环 part Z 必须坚固，扣住腰带不折断）.",
"answer": "(a) Flexibility.\n  (b)(i) A belt. As K is the most flexible it must be able to wrap around a person's waist.\n  (b)(ii) Strength. It is strong.",
"keypoints": "(a) Keyword \"flexibility\"\n(b) i) Key point: K has the largest d = most flexible\n(b) The belt must be able to \"wrap around the waist\" (go around the waist\n(b) ii) Keyword \"strength\" (part Z, the buckle, must be strong",
