"stem": "<p>Five pieces of materials were tested for their strength. Each piece of material was hung on a hook. Weights were added to the other hook hung from the material until the material broke.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA2_AiTong/q6_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Set-up diagram — a hook under a wooden board, with a strip of material hung on the hook, and weights hung from the other end of the material by another hook.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>The graph below shows the number of weights needed to break each material.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA2_AiTong/q6_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Bar chart of \"Number of weights\" (vertical axis 0–6) for materials J, K, L, M, N: J about 4.5, K about 2.5, L about 5.5 (highest), M about 1.5 (lowest), N about 3.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>(a) Which is the strongest material? [1]</p>\n<p>(b) State the material(s) that is/are stronger and weaker than K. [2]</p>\n<p>Stronger than K: ________</p>\n<p>Weaker than K: ________</p>",
