"difficulty": 3,
"kw": "",
"stem": "<p><strong>(a)</strong> Study the flowchart on materials.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA2_MahaBodhi/q9_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Classification flow chart of materials: Materials → Is it flexible? Yes→D; No→ Is it waterproof? Yes→ Does it break easily? Yes→C, No→B; No→A.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>(a) Based on the flowchart, state all the properties of material A.　[2]<br>- Property 1: ________<br>- Property 2: ________</p>\n<p><strong>(b)</strong> Janet conducted an experiment to test the strength of three different materials, E, F and G. The materials are of the same thickness and length.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA2_MahaBodhi/q9_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A strip of material is clamped on a retort stand, with a weight hanging below it.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Weights were added one by one to the material. The number of weights added before it broke is shown in the graph below.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA2_MahaBodhi/q9_fig3.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Bar chart: E held 7 weights, F held 4, G held 10.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>(i) Based on the graph above, arrange the materials, E, F and G, based on their strength from the strongest to the weakest.　[1]</p>\n<p>(ii) Janet wanted a band to tie up her book as shown below.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA2_MahaBodhi/q9_fig4.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A book tied up with a band.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Besides not breaking easily, what is another property that the band must have?　[1]</p>",
"options": [],
"myAnswer": "- (a) Property 1: It is not waterproof. Property 2: It is not flexible.\n  - (b)(i) G（strongest）→ E → F（weakest）\n  - (b)(ii) It must be flexible（能弯曲绕住书）。",
"answer": "- (a) Property 1: Material A is not waterproof. Property 2: Material A is not flexible.\n  - (b)(i) G, E, F\n  - (b)(ii) Flexibility. It is flexible.",
