"subtopic": "Magnets",
"difficulty": 3,
"kw": "",
"stem": "<p>Sean wanted to find out how the number of coils of wire around an iron nail affects the strength of an electromagnet using the set up shown below.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA2_MahaBodhi/q12_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Set-up: a battery connected by wire wound around an iron nail, with steel needles in a tray below the nail.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>He recorded his observations in the table below.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA2_MahaBodhi/q12_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Table: Number of coils of wire — 10 → 8 needles; 20 → 15; 30 → 23.</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>(a)</strong> State what would happen to the steel needles that were attracted to the electromagnet when the battery is removed.　[1]</p>\n<p><strong>(b)</strong> Based on the results, how does increasing the number of coils of wire around the iron nail affect the strength of the electromagnet?　[1]</p>\n<p><strong>(c)</strong> Sean added another battery to his set up with 30 coils of wire around his iron nail as shown in the diagram below.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA2_MahaBodhi/q12_fig3.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>The set-up is changed to two batteries connected in series in the circuit, with an iron nail wound with 30 coils of wire.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Would Sean observe more, fewer or similar number of pins attracted by the electromagnet? Explain your answer.　[1]</p>",
"options": [],
"myAnswer": "- (a) The steel needles will drop / no longer be attracted（电磁铁失去磁性）。\n  - (b) The more coils of wire, the stronger the electromagnet（吸引的钢针更多）。\n  - (c) More pins — two batteries give more (stronger) current, making the electromagnet stronger.",
"answer": "- (a) The steel needles will not be attracted to the iron nail.\n  - (b) The more the number of coils of wire, the stronger the electromagnet.\n  - (c) More pins will be attracted, it would create more electromagnetic strength.",
