"kw": "",
"stem": "<p>Peter wanted to make a bench for his family to sit on.<br>He tested three materials, W, X and Y, used as part A of the bench.<br>He placed a 200 kg weight on each material and recorded his observations in the table below.<br>(a) Which of the materials, W, X, or Y, is most suitable for Peter to use for part A of the bench? Explain your answer. [2]<br>(b) How would the distance d be affected if a lighter weight is used? [1]</p>\n<figure>- <img src=\"images/WA2_NanHua/q8_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Diagram: Q8 bench, with part A (the seat) labelled</figcaption></figure>\n<figure>- <img src=\"images/WA2_NanHua/q8_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Diagram: Q8 test set-up (a 200 kg weight pressing on a material supported at both ends, with d the distance it bends down) and data table for W/X/Y (d of 8 cm, 1 cm and 10 cm respectively)</figcaption></figure>",
"options": [],
"myAnswer": "- (a) Material X. 加入同样的 200 kg 重物后，X 的下弯距离 d 最小（1 cm，W 为 8 cm、Y 为 10 cm），说明 X 最硬、最不易弯曲，坐上人后椅面不会下陷，所以最适合做 part A。\n  - (b) d would decrease.（重量越轻，材料下弯越少，d 变小。）",
"answer": "- **8a** Material X (Choice)\n    - Distance d is the least. (Evidence)\n    - so material X is the most rigid / least flexible. (Concept)\n    - Thus the bench will not bend / sink under the weight of the people sitting on it. (Link)\n  - **8b** d would decrease.",
