"stem": "<p>Rods W, X and Y have the same thickness but are made of different materials. A similar weight is hung on each rod as shown in the set-up below.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA2_Rosyth/q11_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>\n<p>(Caption: experimental set-up — a rod resting on two supports, with a weight hung in the middle using a string)</p>\n<p>The diagram below shows how the three rods look like when the weight is hanging on it.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA2_Rosyth/q11_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>\n<p>(Caption: rod W bent slightly downwards; rod X hardly bent (straight); rod Y bent clearly downwards (bent the most))</p>\n<p>Which of the following statements is correct?</p>",
"options": [
{
"label": "1",
"text": "Rod Y is the strongest."
},
{
"label": "2",
"text": "Rod X is the strongest."
},
{
"label": "3",
"text": "Rod W is less flexible than rod Y."
},
{
"label": "4",
"text": "Rod X is more flexible than rod Y."
}
],
"myAnswer": "(3)",
"answer": "(3)",
"keypoints": "Correct option (3) — Rod W is less flexible than rod Y.",
