"subtopic": "Materials",
"difficulty": 3,
"kw": "",
"stem": "<p>Marcus set up an experiment to test the strength of three materials L, M and N. He hung blocks of the same mass on the rope, one at a time, until it broke.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA2_Rosyth/q17_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>\n<p>(Caption: set-up — a support at the top, a strip of material M hung in the middle, with a block attached at the bottom)</p>\n<p>His results are shown in the table below.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA2_Rosyth/q17_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>\n<p>(Caption: results table — L: 5 blocks; M: 9 blocks; N: 7 blocks (number of blocks added before the strip broke))</p>\n<p>(a) Based on Marcus' results, arrange the materials, L, M and N, from the strongest to the weakest. [1]</p>\n<p>____ , ____ , ____<br>(strongest)　　　(weakest)</p>\n<p>The fishes caught by the fishermen are very heavy.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA2_Rosyth/q17_fig3.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>\n<p>(Caption: a fisherman casting a fishing net from a boat, arrow pointing to the fishing net)</p>\n<p>(b) Based on Marcus' results, which material, L, M or N, is most suitable to be used to make the fishing net below? Explain your answer. [2]</p>\n<p>Fishermen hang their fishing nets on drying racks to dry under the sun as shown in the diagram above.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA2_Rosyth/q17_fig4.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>\n<p>(Caption: fishing nets hung on drying racks to dry)</p>\n<p>(c) What property of material must the fishing net have to be hung on the rack? [1]</p>",
"options": [],
"myAnswer": "(a) M, N, L\n  (b) Material M, because it held the most blocks (9) before breaking, so it is the strongest and can hold the weight of the heavy fish without breaking.\n  (c) It must be flexible.",
