"kw": "",
"stem": "<p>The diagram below shows the life cycle of a butterfly.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA3_MGS/q12_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>\n<p>(a) Why does the butterfly lay eggs on leaves? [1]</p>\n<p>(b) State <strong>two</strong> differences between the larva and pupa stages in the life cycle of a butterfly. [2]<br>(i) ______________________________<br>(ii) ______________________________</p>",
"options": [],
"myAnswer": "(a) So that when the eggs hatch, the larvae (caterpillars) can feed on the leaves for food.\n  (b) (i) The larva feeds on food/eats but the pupa does not eat.\n      (ii) The larva moves/crawls from place to place but the pupa does not move.",
"answer": "(a) To ensure the larva will have food to feed on when the egg hatches.\n  (b) (i) The larva feeds on food while the pupa does not.\n      (ii) The larva moves from place to place while the pupa does not.",
