"stem": "<p>Jia Jia dipped four strips of different materials, A, B, C and D, into a tank containing coloured water as shown.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA3_NanHua/q8_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Strips A, B, C and D of material held by a clip on a stand, with their lower ends dipped into a tank of coloured water.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>After 10 minutes, she took the strips out of the tank and measured the height that the coloured water had travelled. The results are shown below.</p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA3_NanHua/q8_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Heights that the coloured water rose: Material A/B/C/D = 1 / 10 / 7 / 4 cm.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>(a) Based on Jia Jia's experimental results, which material, A, B, C or D, would be most suitable for making a bath towel? Explain your answer. [2]</p>\n<p>(b) Other than the physical property tested in the experiment, state another property a bath towel must have to wrap around our body. [1]</p>",
