"stem": "<p><strong>Part I (10 marks)</strong><br>Read the instructions and carry out the investigation.<br><strong>Task 1: Compare the different objects and classify them into magnetic and non-magnetic groups</strong><br><strong>[Procedure]</strong><br>1. Remove magnet A and objects, P, Q, R and S from the plastic bag.<br>2. Place P, Q, R and S on your table.<br>3. Hold magnet A above each object one at a time.<br>4. Observe what happens to each object and record your observations in (a).<br><strong>[Results]</strong><br>(a) Put a tick (√) if the object moved towards magnet A and (X) if the object did not move. <strong>[2]</strong><br>(b) Based on your experimental results in (a), classify the objects, P, Q, R and S in the table below. <strong>[2]</strong></p>\n<table><tbody><tr><td>Objects</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Magnetic</td><td>Non-magnetic</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>(c) P, Q, R and S, can also be classified as shown in the classification chart below. Study the classification chart and suggest suitable headings. <strong>[1]</strong></p>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA3_Rosyth/qT1_fig1.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>\n<figure><img src=\"images/WA3_Rosyth/qT1_fig2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>",
